1
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,200
Don't you have a friend working at State Security?

2
00:01:40,319 --> 00:01:42,120
Can you help me check his background?

3
00:01:42,439 --> 00:01:43,760
Have you noticed something?

4
00:01:44,239 --> 00:01:45,400
Nothing much.

5
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:48,000
You know how people from Taiwan, China are.

6
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,439
You can't trust a word he says.

7
00:01:49,439 --> 00:01:51,000
Just to turn a profit in business,

8
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,359
they'll do just about anything.

9
00:01:52,599 --> 00:01:54,599
It never hurts to be cautious.

10
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:58,519
Tell your brother-in-law the truth.

11
00:02:02,519 --> 00:02:03,920
Are you with State Security?

12
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:06,560
You are, aren't you?

13
00:02:06,959 --> 00:02:08,000
If I were with State Security,

14
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:09,840
I would've arrested Lin Kanshan long ago.

15
00:02:10,759 --> 00:02:12,199
I really wish you were.

16
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:18,000
All right, all right, Mr. Lin.

17
00:02:20,439 --> 00:02:22,039
Then we'll proceed

18
00:02:23,479 --> 00:02:25,280
in the direction we discussed today,

19
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:27,199
and move forward with it.

20
00:02:27,199 --> 00:02:27,840
No problem.

21
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:29,400
As for the details, I'll have...

22
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:31,719
my secretary sort and send them to yours.

23
00:02:31,719 --> 00:02:33,039
They'll follow up on it, all right?

24
00:02:33,319 --> 00:02:35,560
Mr. Lin, we go back a long way.

25
00:02:35,759 --> 00:02:36,879
Just leave it to me, don't worry.

26
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:38,599
Good, good, good.

27
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:39,919
Much obliged, then.

28
00:02:40,199 --> 00:02:41,439
Goodbye, goodbye.

29
00:02:41,759 --> 00:02:43,080
Pleasure doing business, Boss Lin.

30
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:44,199
To prosperity!

31
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:45,120
Smooth sailing.

32
00:02:45,319 --> 00:02:46,080
To fortune.

33
00:02:52,919 --> 00:02:54,879
Brother Qi, what a coincidence.

34
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:57,199
Where've you been making bank lately?

35
00:02:57,479 --> 00:02:58,639
How do you have the time

36
00:02:58,639 --> 00:03:00,360
to come here for drinks and the view?

37
00:03:08,919 --> 00:03:11,159
Wu Jinhe isn't as cautious as before.

38
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:14,199
What you've done recently is sensitive.

39
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:18,159
If I were you, I wouldn't leave.

40
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:21,039
Without evidence, nobody can arrest you.

41
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:22,240
In other words,

42
00:03:22,599 --> 00:03:24,360
they would've arrested you already.

43
00:03:25,039 --> 00:03:26,080
Do you understand what I mean?

44
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,439
I was just wondering...

45
00:03:38,759 --> 00:03:40,560
For this life-saving debt of gratitude,

46
00:03:40,919 --> 00:03:42,319
how could I ever repay you?

47
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:45,599
Buy me a drink.

48
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:50,240
You can owe me for now.

49
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:21,839
Brother Wen,

50
00:04:23,319 --> 00:04:25,279
that boss you mentioned last time,

51
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,600
named Lin, or was it Wu—

52
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:29,839
wasn't he looking to acquire a hotel here?

53
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:31,879
Did he ever get back in touch with you?

54
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:36,079
I'm serious.

55
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:39,759
I'm going into overseas immigration.

56
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:41,240
Could you ask him for me

57
00:04:41,639 --> 00:04:43,279
if he's interested in buying my company?

58
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:14,199
The number you dialed is currently unan—

59
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:21,160
Hello?

60
00:05:21,959 --> 00:05:22,920
Is this the disability center?

61
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,360
Could you check for me...

62
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:27,480
if Lin Zude in Ward 3 is asleep?

63
00:05:27,879 --> 00:05:29,120
Why isn't he answering his phone?

64
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:30,959
I'm his son.

65
00:05:32,839 --> 00:05:34,199
A blood clot in his brain?

66
00:05:35,639 --> 00:05:37,160
Why didn't anyone tell me?

67
00:05:38,519 --> 00:05:39,959
All right, never mind all that now.

68
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:41,079
How is he doing now?

69
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:44,720
I'm booking a flight right now.

70
00:05:57,279 --> 00:05:58,639
When will Old Wei get here?

71
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:00,120
Probably on his way.

72
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:00,959
Should be soon.

73
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:04,480
What do you think?

74
00:06:04,959 --> 00:06:06,360
Where do the higher-ups stand?

75
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,120
If you were Old Wei,

76
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:09,920
would you take the initiative

77
00:06:10,199 --> 00:06:11,560
to move against Lin Kanshan?

78
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,839
We can move against him anytime.

79
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:17,680
There's no need to do it today.

80
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:18,920
It'll spook the target.

81
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:21,240
Catch him, and the rest will scatter.

82
00:06:21,519 --> 00:06:23,639
But if he leaves now,

83
00:06:23,759 --> 00:06:25,040
what if he never comes back?

84
00:06:25,319 --> 00:06:26,079
Impossible.

85
00:06:26,879 --> 00:06:28,439
This time is different.

86
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,879
His life's work and assets are all here.

87
00:06:30,959 --> 00:06:32,160
He wouldn't just abandon them.

88
00:06:33,839 --> 00:06:34,600
That's true.

89
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:37,800
I called Taipei as well.

90
00:06:38,279 --> 00:06:39,439
His father's condition is real.

91
00:06:39,759 --> 00:06:41,399
The Cultural and Trade Forum is days away.

92
00:06:41,720 --> 00:06:43,759
He spent nearly six months preparing.

93
00:06:44,079 --> 00:06:45,199
Knowing him,

94
00:06:45,199 --> 00:06:46,600
he'd never give up halfway.

95
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:48,680
In a person's life,

96
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:50,319
it's just a few decades.

97
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:51,839
Only by doing this

98
00:06:52,319 --> 00:06:53,720
can he take control of his fate.

99
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:54,959
Only this way

100
00:06:55,079 --> 00:06:56,279
can he hold his head high

101
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:58,240
before his dad, grandaunt, and ancestors.

102
00:06:58,639 --> 00:06:59,720
Only doing this

103
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:01,800
brings that spark back to his eyes.

104
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:03,839
That does make sense.

105
00:07:04,439 --> 00:07:07,079
Otherwise, he wouldn't be so busy with

106
00:07:07,079 --> 00:07:08,879
the *Dwelling in the Fuchun Mountains*

107
00:07:08,879 --> 00:07:10,319
cross-strait show, a thankless task.

108
00:07:11,759 --> 00:07:12,720
Life is like that.

109
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:13,759
Many things

110
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:16,279
can't be measured purely by calculation.

111
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:17,920
Doing something willingly

112
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:19,120
versus being forced into it—

113
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:20,199
the difference is night and day.

114
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:21,720
If I were Old Wei,

115
00:07:21,879 --> 00:07:23,079
I'd wait until he swims back,

116
00:07:23,279 --> 00:07:24,600
fence in the pond,

117
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:26,000
and catch all the fish in one net.

118
00:07:26,319 --> 00:07:28,439
He's been trying to sell his companies,

119
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,839
but the offers are dirt cheap.

120
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:32,040
I'm guessing

121
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:33,680
he won't be able to sell them soon.

122
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:35,279
What about Qiutian?

123
00:07:35,279 --> 00:07:36,319
Any word from her?

124
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:37,560
Things aren't going well.

125
00:07:37,759 --> 00:07:39,000
I almost slipped up once.

126
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:41,399
Lin Kanshan nearly caught on, too.

127
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:42,399
As for her,

128
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:44,399
she still doesn't trust me.

129
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:45,519
Between the two of us,

130
00:07:45,519 --> 00:07:47,399
there's been friction over the years.

131
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,319
Both in personality and working style,

132
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:52,680
it's been a long adjustment period.

133
00:07:52,959 --> 00:07:54,000
And there's simply no sign

134
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,560
of any progress in sight.

135
00:07:55,839 --> 00:07:57,439
She only trusts her previous contact.

136
00:07:58,079 --> 00:07:59,199
So what do you want to do?

137
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:01,720
I wanted to get your thoughts on it.

138
00:08:02,319 --> 00:08:03,800
Should we cut ties

139
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:05,560
and burn this contact?

140
00:08:13,759 --> 00:08:15,360
Number 331, Liu Fang.

141
00:08:16,279 --> 00:08:17,480
You may go in now.

142
00:08:20,199 --> 00:08:22,120
Number 332, Jin Lina.

143
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:24,399
Jin Lina?

144
00:08:25,519 --> 00:08:26,680
Jin Lina, you're up.

145
00:08:26,879 --> 00:08:27,920
You may go in now.

146
00:08:33,799 --> 00:08:35,200
Jin Lina, unmarried.

147
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:37,159
No family history. Is your family here?

148
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:39,200
Whatever it is, you can just tell me.

149
00:08:40,679 --> 00:08:42,159
Do you drink often?

150
00:08:42,879 --> 00:08:44,639
Yes. Is there a problem?

151
00:08:45,399 --> 00:08:46,840
Mild gastritis,

152
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:48,440
and chronic pharyngitis.

153
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:51,559
Did your partner finish his checkup?

154
00:08:51,559 --> 00:08:52,279
Is he here?

155
00:08:53,159 --> 00:08:54,759
He went out of town.

156
00:08:54,879 --> 00:08:56,240
Probably won't come back.

157
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:58,600
Is something wrong?

158
00:08:59,159 --> 00:09:00,080
With him, or with me?

159
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:01,840
As for your test results,

160
00:09:01,840 --> 00:09:04,720
they show a possible breast issue.

161
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,559
You should visit the cancer hospital

162
00:09:06,879 --> 00:09:07,600
to get checked there,

163
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:08,759
just to confirm it, okay?

164
00:09:28,399 --> 00:09:30,759
Number 335, Lin Jingyi.

165
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,360
You can go in now.

166
00:09:50,120 --> 00:09:51,120
No matter how urgent it is,

167
00:09:51,679 --> 00:09:53,279
we can't contact each other anymore.

168
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:54,240
Whatever you say.

169
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:58,159
If you say no contact, then no contact.

170
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:29,720
You need to do as you're told.

171
00:10:30,279 --> 00:10:32,120
That caregiver was right last time.

172
00:10:32,399 --> 00:10:33,480
The only reason you're in here

173
00:10:33,679 --> 00:10:35,360
is because you wouldn't follow orders.

174
00:10:35,919 --> 00:10:37,600
Always insisting on such salty food.

175
00:10:37,879 --> 00:10:39,120
Now look, you've made it worse again.

176
00:10:39,559 --> 00:10:41,120
This place is a front line too, you know.

177
00:10:41,279 --> 00:10:42,559
The front line of your treatment.

178
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:44,480
So you have to follow orders.

179
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:47,039
If you'd just listened earlier,

180
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:49,279
I wouldn't have had to rush back.

181
00:10:50,279 --> 00:10:51,480
I thought you were dying.

182
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:54,919
Stop grumbling under your breath.

183
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:56,559
Say something. Let me hear you.

184
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:58,440
I did cooperate.

185
00:10:59,519 --> 00:11:00,679
The doctors and nurses

186
00:11:01,039 --> 00:11:02,279
are just passing the buck.

187
00:11:03,159 --> 00:11:05,440
If they can't cure it, they blame me.

188
00:11:05,919 --> 00:11:07,360
When you called,

189
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,440
I was having a catheter put in.

190
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:11,559
How was I supposed to answer?

191
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:14,000
A catheter is one thing,

192
00:11:14,399 --> 00:11:15,840
your head is another.

193
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:17,240
He talks nonsense,

194
00:11:17,440 --> 00:11:18,639
and you just buy it.

195
00:11:19,639 --> 00:11:21,000
A pair of fools.

196
00:11:23,399 --> 00:11:24,440
Still got the energy to curse people out.

197
00:11:24,639 --> 00:11:25,919
You're speaking quite clearly, too.

198
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:28,960
Means the blockage isn't too bad.

199
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:32,080
Where's that chubby caregiver?

200
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:33,080
Why didn't she come?

201
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:34,639
How should I know?

202
00:11:35,279 --> 00:11:36,360
Go ask her yourself.

203
00:11:37,879 --> 00:11:39,559
My teeth are bad.

204
00:11:39,919 --> 00:11:41,559
I can't even chew tofu anymore.

205
00:11:42,200 --> 00:11:44,080
She keeps serving carrots,

206
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:45,480
and they're undercooked, too.

207
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:50,600
We weren't finished talking earlier.

208
00:11:50,919 --> 00:11:52,360
How's your grandaunt doing?

209
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,200
Her teeth,

210
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:55,759
are they still good?

211
00:11:56,159 --> 00:11:57,720
She works in the fields every day.

212
00:11:58,320 --> 00:11:59,559
She's healthier than I am.

213
00:11:59,759 --> 00:12:01,240
I asked the relatives,

214
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:03,200
and they said every day at noon

215
00:12:03,399 --> 00:12:04,559
she still has a cup of liquor.

216
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:05,759
So you don't need to worry about her.

217
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:08,519
This piece is smaller, easier to chew.

218
00:12:08,919 --> 00:12:09,919
Eat slowly.

219
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,600
What about her grandson

220
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:19,559
and her son?

221
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:21,320
Are they good to her?

222
00:12:21,879 --> 00:12:23,080
With me standing right there,

223
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:24,759
they had to put on their best behavior.

224
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:26,679
But I took a close look,

225
00:12:26,919 --> 00:12:28,600
and Grandaunt's clothes and shoes

226
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:29,919
didn't look like they were just for show.

227
00:12:29,919 --> 00:12:31,600
Her hair and face were clean, too.

228
00:12:32,480 --> 00:12:34,080
They're taking good care of her.

229
00:12:35,759 --> 00:12:37,600
Did you see her eat lunch?

230
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:39,600
What did she eat?

231
00:12:39,799 --> 00:12:40,559
Rice noodles.

232
00:12:41,159 --> 00:12:43,080
I even went to the kitchen to check.

233
00:12:43,279 --> 00:12:44,519
There were steamed buns in the pot,

234
00:12:44,519 --> 00:12:45,399
with tofu filling.

235
00:12:45,639 --> 00:12:47,000
They're all very easy to chew.

236
00:12:55,399 --> 00:12:56,080
What's wrong?

237
00:12:59,799 --> 00:13:03,720
I... I've forgotten what she looks like.

238
00:13:07,519 --> 00:13:09,559
She must have forgotten me too.

239
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:12,080
We were supposed to be family,

240
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:14,120
yet I'm here all alone.

241
00:13:15,399 --> 00:13:17,879
I'll never see her again.

242
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:20,080
All right, give me the apple first.

243
00:13:20,080 --> 00:13:21,080
Don't choke on it.

244
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:23,720
Never see her again...

245
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:25,120
Don't cry.

246
00:13:25,919 --> 00:13:27,279
Great-Aunt is doing just fine.

247
00:13:27,519 --> 00:13:28,600
She's doing well, yet you're crying.

248
00:13:29,720 --> 00:13:31,240
I want to go back to the mainland.

249
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:34,480
I want to go back to the mainland.

250
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:37,480
Lying here like this,

251
00:13:39,159 --> 00:13:41,720
the ancestors will blame me.

252
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:45,279
I have to go back.

253
00:13:45,559 --> 00:13:46,360
I have to pay respects to the ancestors.

254
00:13:47,159 --> 00:13:48,840
Go back and kowtow.

255
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:50,720
You can't get so agitated right now.

256
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:51,679
Calm down, okay?

257
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:53,200
I promise you.

258
00:13:53,679 --> 00:13:55,200
Once you've recovered a bit,

259
00:13:55,759 --> 00:13:57,320
I'll take you back.

260
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:58,759
We'll go back and see her, all right?

261
00:13:59,679 --> 00:14:01,399
Nowhere is closer than Minzhong.

262
00:14:02,879 --> 00:14:04,360
Even if you're in a wheelchair then,

263
00:14:05,559 --> 00:14:06,759
I'll still push you back.

264
00:14:06,879 --> 00:14:07,399
All right?

265
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:08,080
All right.

266
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:11,360
By the way,

267
00:14:12,240 --> 00:14:13,039
Great-Aunt said...

268
00:14:13,399 --> 00:14:15,639
I brought back another family tree copy.

269
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:18,159
Let's find ours at home then,

270
00:14:18,159 --> 00:14:19,360
and compare them properly.

271
00:14:20,639 --> 00:14:21,840
What is it?

272
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:23,159
The family tree.

273
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:24,720
Let's get it sorted out right away.

274
00:14:24,879 --> 00:14:25,759
Otherwise, what if...

275
00:14:27,799 --> 00:14:29,120
What... what if what?

276
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:39,080
What if I get muddled

277
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:40,440
and end up losing it?

278
00:14:41,480 --> 00:14:43,360
We won't even know our ancestors' names.

279
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,759
Lili, I'm on an IV drip.

280
00:15:11,399 --> 00:15:13,240
Go check on Zhu Yingjia in bed six.

281
00:15:13,519 --> 00:15:15,279
I think he's ringing his bell, isn't he?

282
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,279
Hearing the nurse call your name,

283
00:15:43,919 --> 00:15:45,559
I thought it was just a namesake.

284
00:15:46,159 --> 00:15:47,320
How did you end up here?

285
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,600
When were you admitted?

286
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:56,480
When did you get back?

287
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:59,440
Isn't your dad at the disability center?

288
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:01,200
Not in the rehab building anymore?

289
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:04,720
My dad's blood vessels are clogged up too.

290
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:06,399
What about you? Is it serious?

291
00:16:08,679 --> 00:16:11,679
Mainland goal: 50 years of healthy work.

292
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:13,000
They were worried I'd stop working,

293
00:16:13,159 --> 00:16:15,000
so they made me take leave for a checkup.

294
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:16,000
If I don't use it now,

295
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,320
it'll all go to waste.

296
00:16:18,039 --> 00:16:19,399
Might as well take advantage of the perk.

297
00:16:19,639 --> 00:16:20,519
Sit down. Come on.

298
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,480
Would you like some water?

299
00:16:24,159 --> 00:16:26,080
You didn't even get anyone to run errands.

300
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:29,799
My dad's ward is right across the hall.

301
00:16:29,799 --> 00:16:31,200
Just call me anytime if you need anything.

302
00:16:31,639 --> 00:16:33,000
Don't worry about that. Sit down, sit.

303
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:38,639
Do you think I'm finished?

304
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:40,000
An old soldier past his prime,

305
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,200
can't even get out of bed?

306
00:16:44,679 --> 00:16:45,720
Of course not.

307
00:16:46,919 --> 00:16:48,279
If something really happened,

308
00:16:48,879 --> 00:16:50,799
I'd be the first to get the call.

309
00:16:51,519 --> 00:16:52,679
To change handlers,

310
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:54,360
wouldn't they still have to

311
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:56,879
notify the subordinates?

312
00:16:57,360 --> 00:16:58,960
Maybe someone can't wait for that.

313
00:16:59,679 --> 00:17:01,039
The sooner, the better, right?

314
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:07,000
You didn't report in first upon returning,

315
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:08,759
but rushed over to see me instead.

316
00:17:09,039 --> 00:17:12,160
People will say you lack tact.

317
00:17:13,039 --> 00:17:13,680
Who is it?

318
00:17:21,839 --> 00:17:22,680
Come in.

319
00:17:29,640 --> 00:17:31,640
The youngest deputy chief in history!

320
00:17:31,640 --> 00:17:32,400
Look at you!

321
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:37,279
If I hadn't gone to see Old Zhu,

322
00:17:37,480 --> 00:17:39,000
I wouldn't even know you got promoted!

323
00:17:39,319 --> 00:17:40,279
Riding a mainland missile

324
00:17:40,279 --> 00:17:41,519
wouldn't be as fast as you!

325
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:42,519
How did you pull it off?

326
00:17:42,640 --> 00:17:44,240
Teach me your secrets!

327
00:17:45,759 --> 00:17:47,200
Whose office was this before?

328
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:51,000
Back when I came to Old Zhu's office

329
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:52,519
to talk business,

330
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:53,920
I had to keep my head down for a lecture.

331
00:17:54,119 --> 00:17:55,480
Never dared to look around.

332
00:17:55,480 --> 00:17:57,119
I never knew what the boss

333
00:17:57,359 --> 00:17:58,440
had in his office.

334
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:02,440
With this door shut,

335
00:18:02,599 --> 00:18:04,279
you could do somersaults in here!

336
00:18:04,519 --> 00:18:05,400
Got any water?

337
00:18:06,279 --> 00:18:08,200
Came all this way, and no tea for me?

338
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:16,400
According to procedure,

339
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:18,319
you should take a polygraph test first.

340
00:18:18,599 --> 00:18:19,839
But I've been swamped,

341
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:21,200
so I called you over

342
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,119
because we need to discuss something.

343
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:23,759
What is it?

344
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:26,559
Didn't I ask you to get the airport land?

345
00:18:26,759 --> 00:18:28,000
You seem to have worked on it for a while,

346
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:29,440
and spent quite a bit of money.

347
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:30,440
Can't get the paperwork approved?

348
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:35,839
It involves the military.

349
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,880
Their barriers are set pretty high.

350
00:18:38,039 --> 00:18:38,799
I have to find a way.

351
00:18:38,799 --> 00:18:39,599
Tasks

352
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:42,400
have priorities.

353
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:45,400
Secure that land at all costs,

354
00:18:46,359 --> 00:18:47,119
and expedite it.

355
00:18:47,359 --> 00:18:49,960
Also, sort out all your accounts,

356
00:18:50,319 --> 00:18:52,599
submit them, the more detailed the better.

357
00:18:52,759 --> 00:18:54,880
You can't just state numbers verbally;

358
00:18:54,960 --> 00:18:55,880
we need itemized details.

359
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:00,160
The accounts?

360
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:03,200
Right. Aren't you running cross-strait exchanges?

361
00:19:03,279 --> 00:19:04,519
The ancient painting exhibition and all...

362
00:19:04,519 --> 00:19:05,960
You didn't pay for that yourself, did you?

363
00:19:06,799 --> 00:19:08,200
Doesn't the company balance its books?

364
00:19:09,519 --> 00:19:12,559
Submit all past revenues and expenses.

365
00:19:12,839 --> 00:19:14,400
We will examine them thoroughly.

366
00:19:14,799 --> 00:19:16,279
Anyway, manage your own schedule,

367
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:17,759
but don't take longer than half a month.

368
00:19:20,519 --> 00:19:21,799
Hand over accounts?

369
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:24,839
We never had to submit them before.

370
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:28,640
The past practice had serious problems.

371
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:32,279
Overstaffed and inefficient,

372
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:35,920
leaving bad debts for others to clean up.

373
00:19:37,400 --> 00:19:38,559
I'm not targeting you.

374
00:19:38,759 --> 00:19:39,440
It's just that

375
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:41,400
everyone has to submit them.

376
00:19:45,319 --> 00:19:46,480
You mean...

377
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:48,000
I've made myself very clear.

378
00:19:48,519 --> 00:19:49,440
If you don't understand,

379
00:19:50,559 --> 00:19:51,759
it means you refuse to listen,

380
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:54,799
or

381
00:19:56,599 --> 00:19:57,559
refuse to comply.

382
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:18,559
If the nurse catches me,

383
00:20:18,559 --> 00:20:20,079
will they lock me up?

384
00:20:28,400 --> 00:20:29,920
One more can won't kill you,

385
00:20:30,079 --> 00:20:32,039
and one less won't get you out sooner.

386
00:20:34,119 --> 00:20:35,559
Wish it were chilled, though.

387
00:20:36,559 --> 00:20:38,519
Next time I'll pack ice cubes in my pants.

388
00:20:38,960 --> 00:20:39,960
If anyone asks,

389
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:41,720
I'll say I'm hurt and need an ice pack.

390
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:46,039
Your corny jokes are getting worse.

391
00:20:46,559 --> 00:20:47,839
You can't even walk straight,

392
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:49,240
yet you're still talking big.

393
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:50,480
How much did you drink before coming?

394
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:51,839
Reporting, sir!

395
00:20:52,599 --> 00:20:53,640
Just a little bit!

396
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:06,720
Chen Leyuan...

397
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:09,079
Did he give you an attitude?

398
00:21:10,799 --> 00:21:11,680
I hear

399
00:21:12,519 --> 00:21:13,920
he's very hardworking,

400
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:15,200
hands-on with everything,

401
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:17,599
and wants to dredge up my old messes.

402
00:21:17,839 --> 00:21:19,200
A new official always sets three fires.

403
00:21:19,200 --> 00:21:20,680
Did the flames scorch your crotch?

404
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:21,799
That bastard.

405
00:21:21,799 --> 00:21:23,720
He's not even fit to shine your shoes.

406
00:21:23,720 --> 00:21:24,599
Making such a big blaze,

407
00:21:24,599 --> 00:21:25,680
he's bound to burn himself.

408
00:21:29,039 --> 00:21:30,559
Do I look terrible?

409
00:21:30,799 --> 00:21:31,839
I've been too tired lately.

410
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:33,279
A little alcohol went to my head.

411
00:21:35,519 --> 00:21:37,359
I hear you've been busy lately.

412
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:39,880
Deputy Secretary-General of the Chamber,

413
00:21:40,799 --> 00:21:43,079
running a Cultural and Trade Forum event,

414
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:44,319
dealing with me,

415
00:21:44,480 --> 00:21:46,880
and now having to handle Chen Leyuan too.

416
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:49,519
Guarding against mainland State Security.

417
00:21:49,720 --> 00:21:50,839
With so much going on,

418
00:21:51,799 --> 00:21:52,920
can you handle it all?

419
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:55,599
For your matters, I give my all.

420
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:58,000
As for the rest,

421
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:03,519
it doesn't matter.

422
00:22:03,759 --> 00:22:05,359
When I was young,

423
00:22:05,559 --> 00:22:06,680
I loved to complain too.

424
00:22:06,799 --> 00:22:08,160
Work is work,

425
00:22:08,279 --> 00:22:10,359
and venting is venting. It's normal.

426
00:22:11,480 --> 00:22:13,640
If someone like Chen Leyuan takes over,

427
00:22:13,759 --> 00:22:15,359
the MIB will be finished.

428
00:22:16,119 --> 00:22:17,599
He advocates Taiwan, China independence.

429
00:22:17,599 --> 00:22:20,279
A politician, an opportunist.

430
00:22:20,279 --> 00:22:21,519
He isn't like us.

431
00:22:21,960 --> 00:22:23,640
What's wrong with politicians?

432
00:22:23,640 --> 00:22:24,640
It all depends on

433
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:27,000
which chair their ass is sitting in,

434
00:22:27,319 --> 00:22:29,119
who feeds them and pays their bills.

435
00:22:29,319 --> 00:22:30,440
It's the KMT right now.

436
00:22:31,240 --> 00:22:31,960
What about next term?

437
00:22:32,240 --> 00:22:33,559
If it's the DPP,

438
00:22:33,559 --> 00:22:34,319
will they pursue independence?

439
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:36,039
Without a doubt.

440
00:22:37,039 --> 00:22:38,079
What are you trying to say?

441
00:22:38,880 --> 00:22:40,279
I've always wanted to ask:

442
00:22:41,440 --> 00:22:43,200
Is Taiwan, China independence really good?

443
00:22:43,960 --> 00:22:46,279
Is it truly good for the ordinary people?

444
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:49,559
Or just for a few politicians' greed?

445
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:51,920
If it's for Taiwan, China's independence,

446
00:22:51,920 --> 00:22:53,119
for those pro-independence politicians'

447
00:22:53,119 --> 00:22:54,160
shameless personal desires,

448
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:55,960
then what about us risking our lives?

449
00:22:55,960 --> 00:22:58,559
What was the point of our struggles?

450
00:23:02,559 --> 00:23:03,440
You're drunk.

451
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:08,759
People like us,

452
00:23:09,079 --> 00:23:10,759
crossing the sea to the mainland,

453
00:23:11,039 --> 00:23:12,319
cheating, stealing, swindling, and lying...

454
00:23:12,480 --> 00:23:14,119
Who knows if we'll open our eyes one day

455
00:23:15,240 --> 00:23:16,599
and wake up behind bars.

456
00:23:16,880 --> 00:23:18,559
Didn't they say they didn't want war?

457
00:23:18,839 --> 00:23:20,759
Yet they tell me to get the airport land.

458
00:23:21,319 --> 00:23:22,480
If it were for Taiwan, China,

459
00:23:22,480 --> 00:23:23,559
I wouldn't care if I died.

460
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:24,920
But if it's for the interests

461
00:23:24,920 --> 00:23:26,400
of those pro-independence politicians,

462
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:27,839
I refuse to accept it.

463
00:23:28,920 --> 00:23:31,640
Chen says Chinese don't fight Chinese,

464
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:33,680
and says he isn't Chinese the next.

465
00:23:33,799 --> 00:23:34,880
Then all our lives we've worshipped

466
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:36,400
Confucius and Lord Guan.

467
00:23:36,400 --> 00:23:37,519
Are they foreigners?

468
00:23:37,759 --> 00:23:39,720
Then who on earth are we?

469
00:23:42,920 --> 00:23:44,599
You have a knot in your heart

470
00:23:45,240 --> 00:23:46,079
that you can't untie.

471
00:23:46,880 --> 00:23:48,599
You said a cross-strait war is inevitable.

472
00:23:48,680 --> 00:23:50,839
We've struggled for 20 years—

473
00:23:51,079 --> 00:23:52,680
who the hell are we fighting for?

474
00:23:53,359 --> 00:23:54,759
What are we fighting for?

475
00:23:57,440 --> 00:23:58,680
We are soldiers.

476
00:23:59,599 --> 00:24:01,240
Orders come before everything.

477
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:03,799
Taiwan, China's interests come first.

478
00:24:03,799 --> 00:24:05,440
What that translates to is:

479
00:24:05,440 --> 00:24:07,000
those politicians need an enemy,

480
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:08,039
they need an opponent,

481
00:24:08,039 --> 00:24:10,480
just to win votes from the electorate.

482
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:11,480
Isn't that right?

483
00:24:15,799 --> 00:24:17,640
Decades have passed,

484
00:24:18,519 --> 00:24:21,000
and Communist propaganda is still potent.

485
00:24:21,279 --> 00:24:23,039
Even you've been brainwashed.

486
00:24:23,039 --> 00:24:23,720
If you can't figure this out,

487
00:24:23,720 --> 00:24:24,599
then stay behind this time.

488
00:24:24,599 --> 00:24:25,759
Don't go back to the mainland.

489
00:24:31,440 --> 00:24:33,519
Obeying orders is our duty, after all.

490
00:24:34,559 --> 00:24:35,839
You told me to vent,

491
00:24:35,839 --> 00:24:37,599
so I'm giving it to you straight.

492
00:24:37,599 --> 00:24:39,279
Chen Leyuan wants to audit my books.

493
00:24:39,279 --> 00:24:40,559
He wants all my profits

494
00:24:40,559 --> 00:24:41,440
handed over.

495
00:24:41,440 --> 00:24:42,160
Am I supposed to

496
00:24:42,160 --> 00:24:43,279
take this Rolex you gave me

497
00:24:43,279 --> 00:24:44,359
and turn it in, too?

498
00:24:44,359 --> 00:24:45,720
He's even pinning labels on me,

499
00:24:45,720 --> 00:24:46,839
saying I'm your man.

500
00:24:46,839 --> 00:24:48,440
He's staging a purge!

501
00:24:53,240 --> 00:24:54,799
Doing business on the mainland

502
00:24:55,279 --> 00:24:56,079
is tough.

503
00:24:56,359 --> 00:24:57,880
Drinking round after round every day,

504
00:24:57,880 --> 00:24:59,599
entertaining county and township chiefs.

505
00:24:59,599 --> 00:25:00,920
With so many projects,

506
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:03,079
chasing debts isn't easy.

507
00:25:04,680 --> 00:25:06,160
Don't ruin your health drinking.

508
00:25:10,200 --> 00:25:13,000
Someone tailed me to the hospital today.

509
00:25:13,960 --> 00:25:14,799
Very professional.

510
00:25:15,839 --> 00:25:18,640
One of our own tailing another? Why?

511
00:25:22,279 --> 00:25:23,400
You failed your polygraph test.

512
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:24,559
That's the only explanation.

513
00:25:26,599 --> 00:25:27,759
If you're not going back,

514
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:29,200
then I'm done too.

515
00:25:29,359 --> 00:25:30,200
I'll resign.

516
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:32,680
I'll set up a stall and fry rice noodles.

517
00:25:32,920 --> 00:25:33,960
It's still a living.

518
00:25:34,519 --> 00:25:35,880
This boat is small,

519
00:25:37,720 --> 00:25:39,079
but once you get on,

520
00:25:39,519 --> 00:25:41,119
you can never get off.

521
00:25:43,759 --> 00:25:45,240
Tomorrow,

522
00:25:46,160 --> 00:25:47,759
I'll go back to process the paperwork.

523
00:25:48,359 --> 00:25:49,240
I'm retiring.

524
00:25:49,599 --> 00:25:50,839
I got you onto this boat,

525
00:25:52,359 --> 00:25:54,119
yet I'm stepping off first.

526
00:25:56,640 --> 00:25:57,480
I'm sorry.

527
00:26:19,920 --> 00:26:23,640
Eggshell cracks don't form overnight.

528
00:26:24,359 --> 00:26:25,480
It was already there before,

529
00:26:26,039 --> 00:26:27,480
which is why it kept getting wider.

530
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:31,000
Didn't Comrade Zhu Yingjia give a warning?

531
00:26:32,960 --> 00:26:34,279
Where is this person now?

532
00:26:34,559 --> 00:26:35,359
At the hospital.

533
00:26:35,880 --> 00:26:37,079
With Section Chief Zhu.

534
00:26:39,559 --> 00:26:41,079
I thought coming to the "MIB"

535
00:26:41,519 --> 00:26:42,640
was to gather intelligence,

536
00:26:43,079 --> 00:26:44,599
yet I just open packages here every day.

537
00:26:45,279 --> 00:26:46,440
Are you stupid?

538
00:26:46,440 --> 00:26:48,480
They're packages to and from the mainland!

539
00:26:48,480 --> 00:26:50,200
All the secrets are inside.

540
00:26:52,960 --> 00:26:53,720
Be careful.

541
00:26:53,720 --> 00:26:54,839
Don't damage them as you open them.

542
00:26:58,839 --> 00:27:00,079
As for someone restless,

543
00:27:02,559 --> 00:27:04,680
just send him back to open packages.

544
00:28:20,880 --> 00:28:21,680
Director.

545
00:28:22,079 --> 00:28:23,359
When did you get back?

546
00:28:23,720 --> 00:28:25,400
You could've just called me for anything.

547
00:28:25,400 --> 00:28:26,799
There was no need to come in person.

548
00:28:27,319 --> 00:28:28,599
How is your health holding up?

549
00:28:28,599 --> 00:28:30,799
I can still walk, still pay a visit,

550
00:28:30,799 --> 00:28:32,240
and my mouth is still plenty sharp.

551
00:28:32,599 --> 00:28:33,599
Didn't expect that, did you?

552
00:28:35,279 --> 00:28:36,240
Director, please take a seat.

553
00:28:36,240 --> 00:28:37,319
I'll pour you some tea.

554
00:28:37,640 --> 00:28:39,200
Just the other day, I told godmother

555
00:28:39,319 --> 00:28:41,480
that good fortune was smiling upon you,

556
00:28:41,799 --> 00:28:43,640
and the hospital trip was just a checkup.

557
00:28:43,640 --> 00:28:44,839
I heard

558
00:28:46,079 --> 00:28:48,079
you want to pull out all my plants,

559
00:28:48,079 --> 00:28:49,680
root and branch. Is that true?

560
00:28:52,640 --> 00:28:53,440
Well, here's the thing.

561
00:28:53,960 --> 00:28:54,640
Regarding this matter,

562
00:28:54,640 --> 00:28:56,839
I wanted to wait for you to discuss it,

563
00:28:56,839 --> 00:28:58,559
but the higher-ups were in such a rush

564
00:28:58,559 --> 00:29:00,039
that they demanded a proposal from me.

565
00:29:00,400 --> 00:29:01,960
Operation Spring Thunder on the mainland

566
00:29:01,960 --> 00:29:03,960
strikes like thunder every other day.

567
00:29:04,240 --> 00:29:05,680
Our people can't get back,

568
00:29:05,960 --> 00:29:07,799
and honestly, most have been caught.

569
00:29:07,799 --> 00:29:08,960
Then tell me,

570
00:29:09,599 --> 00:29:11,599
does "most" mean many or few?

571
00:29:13,319 --> 00:29:15,839
So young, yet playing these games with me.

572
00:29:16,519 --> 00:29:17,480
Looking me right in the eye,

573
00:29:17,480 --> 00:29:19,119
and you're still putting on an act!

574
00:29:20,079 --> 00:29:22,160
Do you know how hard it was to plant them?

575
00:29:22,319 --> 00:29:23,759
They are like ginseng fruit,

576
00:29:23,960 --> 00:29:25,200
flowering once every thousand years,

577
00:29:25,200 --> 00:29:26,519
bearing fruit once every thousand years.

578
00:29:27,039 --> 00:29:28,200
Who gave you the hoe

579
00:29:28,200 --> 00:29:30,079
to chop the tree and dig up its roots?

580
00:29:30,480 --> 00:29:31,799
Chen Leyuan, what are you doing?

581
00:29:31,960 --> 00:29:33,400
Trying to usurp my position?

582
00:29:33,880 --> 00:29:35,440
I'm not bedridden yet,

583
00:29:35,559 --> 00:29:37,519
and you couldn't even wait a single week!

584
00:29:39,319 --> 00:29:41,640
Zheng Guiping must be losing his sight

585
00:29:42,039 --> 00:29:44,680
to put you in charge of Division Four!

586
00:29:45,039 --> 00:29:46,240
You'd better get one thing straight.

587
00:29:46,559 --> 00:29:48,519
What does "acting head" even mean?

588
00:29:48,599 --> 00:29:51,359
Wiping your superior's ass for a few days,

589
00:29:51,480 --> 00:29:53,200
and you might end up covered in shit!

590
00:29:53,200 --> 00:29:54,839
What bullshit deputy director are you?

591
00:29:54,920 --> 00:29:56,119
Where's your official appointment?

592
00:29:58,480 --> 00:30:00,039
An acting head

593
00:30:01,039 --> 00:30:02,240
is still the head.

594
00:30:02,400 --> 00:30:04,200
As for an official appointment,

595
00:30:04,640 --> 00:30:06,200
that's up to the higher-ups.

596
00:30:06,799 --> 00:30:07,880
You don't need to trouble yourself.

597
00:30:12,079 --> 00:30:13,680
What did you just say?

598
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:16,240
I'm talking about the rules.

599
00:30:17,559 --> 00:30:20,000
Zheng wants you to give me Project Abyss.

600
00:30:20,680 --> 00:30:21,920
A formal handover.

601
00:30:28,519 --> 00:30:29,640
A file like that,

602
00:30:30,640 --> 00:30:32,839
I'll only hand to the Director in person.

603
00:30:33,039 --> 00:30:34,440
If he's gone senile

604
00:30:34,720 --> 00:30:36,440
and wants to give it to any nobody,

605
00:30:37,079 --> 00:30:38,559
that's his business.

606
00:30:50,200 --> 00:30:52,920
Section Chief Zhu retires tomorrow.

607
00:30:53,079 --> 00:30:54,160
Starting now,

608
00:30:54,400 --> 00:30:56,279
revoke his 24 security clearances.

609
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:03,880
Four people

610
00:31:05,559 --> 00:31:06,440
20 years

611
00:31:12,400 --> 00:31:16,519
The tadpoles finally turned into frogs,

612
00:31:17,200 --> 00:31:18,680
and you just abandon them like that?

613
00:31:19,160 --> 00:31:21,119
Plus those locked up in mainland prisons,

614
00:31:21,359 --> 00:31:22,920
we could seat a mahjong table.

615
00:31:23,680 --> 00:31:24,720
Such a waste.

616
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:28,319
Aren't we burning a few too many people?

617
00:31:28,880 --> 00:31:30,359
If nobody's willing to sacrifice the bait,

618
00:31:31,920 --> 00:31:34,160
we'll never catch the wolf in our den.

619
00:31:34,960 --> 00:31:36,000
Like you said,

620
00:31:36,880 --> 00:31:38,079
it's been nearly 20 years.

621
00:31:39,480 --> 00:31:41,759
This mole has been beside us all along.

622
00:31:42,640 --> 00:31:43,440
In another three months,

623
00:31:43,440 --> 00:31:45,000
even you'll have retired.

624
00:31:45,440 --> 00:31:46,720
And he still hasn't surfaced.

625
00:31:48,559 --> 00:31:50,079
If we don't pay a real price now,

626
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:51,799
do you expect

627
00:31:52,720 --> 00:31:54,559
us to take this secret to our graves?

628
00:31:57,599 --> 00:31:59,160
And it's not just four.

629
00:31:59,680 --> 00:32:00,880
Including you,

630
00:32:03,359 --> 00:32:05,200
that's five brothers I must sacrifice!

631
00:32:06,039 --> 00:32:07,559
Sir, I've got an idea.

632
00:32:07,920 --> 00:32:09,640
There's a Communist mole at the top.

633
00:32:10,279 --> 00:32:11,599
The only way to smoke him out

634
00:32:11,759 --> 00:32:12,960
is to use a sacrificial spy.

635
00:32:13,279 --> 00:32:13,960
Go on.

636
00:32:15,640 --> 00:32:19,440
Including Lin Kanshan and in-house agents,

637
00:32:20,039 --> 00:32:21,720
their files and dossiers

638
00:32:21,720 --> 00:32:23,200
are what the Communists need most

639
00:32:23,680 --> 00:32:25,440
and want most desperately.

640
00:32:26,119 --> 00:32:27,920
So we must make the act convincing.

641
00:32:28,680 --> 00:32:30,400
First, spread rumors

642
00:32:30,680 --> 00:32:33,079
that my health is failing,

643
00:32:33,480 --> 00:32:34,720
that I'm stepping down,

644
00:32:35,799 --> 00:32:36,559
and my work is to be handed over,

645
00:32:36,559 --> 00:32:37,599
but I refuse to let go.

646
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:40,480
So you've been searching for a successor.

647
00:32:40,799 --> 00:32:42,559
Chen Leyuan cozying up to the director!

648
00:32:43,559 --> 00:32:45,039
It's great to be young.

649
00:32:45,359 --> 00:32:47,200
Climbing the ladder fast on all fours.

650
00:32:47,359 --> 00:32:49,799
Rumors are going around about your health,

651
00:32:49,960 --> 00:32:52,000
and you even sneaked to get your results.

652
00:32:52,480 --> 00:32:53,839
Do you think he made it up?

653
00:32:54,279 --> 00:32:55,240
Definitely.

654
00:32:56,559 --> 00:32:58,920
All to lure that mole into stealing intel.

655
00:32:58,920 --> 00:32:59,319
Yeah.

656
00:33:00,039 --> 00:33:01,319
Then what about the fake list?

657
00:33:01,319 --> 00:33:02,599
Not fake. It has to be real.

658
00:33:03,160 --> 00:33:04,200
If necessary,

659
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:06,240
we must sacrifice a few

660
00:33:06,480 --> 00:33:08,160
of the real seeds planted in the mainland.

661
00:33:09,200 --> 00:33:10,480
Only an authentic list

662
00:33:10,680 --> 00:33:12,559
will truly convince that mole.

663
00:33:13,319 --> 00:33:15,039
We must make him believe I'm retiring

664
00:33:15,039 --> 00:33:16,160
and never coming back.

665
00:33:16,400 --> 00:33:18,079
Only then will he risk stealing the one

666
00:33:18,079 --> 00:33:19,440
to be handed over to the next person,

667
00:33:19,440 --> 00:33:21,400
that top-secret list in hand.

668
00:33:22,519 --> 00:33:23,960
He only has this one chance.

669
00:33:24,480 --> 00:33:25,440
As soon as this list

670
00:33:25,880 --> 00:33:28,079
with real names leaks out,

671
00:33:28,920 --> 00:33:31,440
my suspect will be confirmed as the mole.

672
00:33:31,960 --> 00:33:33,599
What if it's not him?

673
00:33:36,519 --> 00:33:37,599
I've done this all my life.

674
00:33:38,240 --> 00:33:39,240
If it really isn't him,

675
00:33:39,920 --> 00:33:41,000
it only proves

676
00:33:41,160 --> 00:33:43,039
Old Zhu has gone blind and useless,

677
00:33:43,039 --> 00:33:44,359
and it really is time to retire.

678
00:33:48,160 --> 00:33:49,400
What do you want me to do?

679
00:33:51,279 --> 00:33:52,359
You watch me,

680
00:33:52,440 --> 00:33:53,519
I watch you,

681
00:33:53,599 --> 00:33:54,640
we watch each other.

682
00:33:54,839 --> 00:33:58,599
You play the petty, despicable boss,

683
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:00,599
and preserve my glorious reputation.

684
00:34:01,039 --> 00:34:02,880
I'll have to trouble you to suffer, sir.

685
00:34:05,359 --> 00:34:06,960
The successor must be kept in the dark,

686
00:34:07,640 --> 00:34:08,679
and put to good use.

687
00:34:09,320 --> 00:34:10,400
Do you have someone in mind?

688
00:34:12,159 --> 00:34:13,280
Zhu Yingjia

689
00:34:13,960 --> 00:34:15,239
is wiretapping you.

690
00:34:15,800 --> 00:34:16,760
Chen Leyuan.

691
00:34:17,239 --> 00:34:18,440
Among all these young people,

692
00:34:18,559 --> 00:34:19,960
he's the most eager to climb the ladder.

693
00:34:20,599 --> 00:34:21,679
He spares no scheming,

694
00:34:21,920 --> 00:34:22,840
and stops at nothing.

695
00:34:23,880 --> 00:34:25,519
Why these four?

696
00:34:26,519 --> 00:34:27,480
Why not someone else?

697
00:34:27,880 --> 00:34:29,960
From my first day on the job,

698
00:34:30,880 --> 00:34:32,840
I faced a philosophical question.

699
00:34:33,480 --> 00:34:35,239
Everyone in the espionage world

700
00:34:36,280 --> 00:34:38,039
faces the exact same doubt.

701
00:34:39,320 --> 00:34:41,119
When you release a kite,

702
00:34:42,199 --> 00:34:44,159
and it drifts across the sea,

703
00:34:44,480 --> 00:34:47,039
the string stays in your hand.

704
00:34:47,800 --> 00:34:48,920
But where is its heart?

705
00:34:49,920 --> 00:34:50,920
In the end,

706
00:34:51,119 --> 00:34:52,480
is he an enemy,

707
00:34:52,840 --> 00:34:54,320
or still one of us?

708
00:34:54,920 --> 00:34:57,360
So you've always been on guard,

709
00:34:58,639 --> 00:35:00,559
wary of that mountain.

710
00:35:03,760 --> 00:35:04,800
Honestly,

711
00:35:06,079 --> 00:35:07,360
after nearly 20 years,

712
00:35:09,559 --> 00:35:10,840
even I don't know

713
00:35:11,400 --> 00:35:12,960
if he's still on our side.

714
00:35:13,360 --> 00:35:16,400
Like Ma Qi crossing over to Taiwan, China,

715
00:35:16,800 --> 00:35:17,920
I have no idea

716
00:35:19,119 --> 00:35:21,400
if our comrades far away on the mainland

717
00:35:22,039 --> 00:35:25,159
might have been turned or defected.

718
00:35:26,800 --> 00:35:27,760
Then what about Ma Qi?

719
00:35:28,559 --> 00:35:30,880
How can you know whose side he's on?

720
00:35:31,840 --> 00:35:33,199
So, you can't fully trust anyone.

721
00:35:35,559 --> 00:35:37,239
Perhaps that's the life of a spy.

722
00:35:37,760 --> 00:35:38,719
Once you board that boat,

723
00:35:40,320 --> 00:35:42,599
you're doomed to drift untrusted.

724
00:35:46,880 --> 00:35:48,079
Brother,

725
00:35:48,800 --> 00:35:50,679
in this building,

726
00:35:51,239 --> 00:35:52,719
I've worked for decades.

727
00:35:53,440 --> 00:35:54,679
I've watched

728
00:35:55,079 --> 00:35:57,800
how things changed with the mainland.

729
00:35:58,440 --> 00:35:59,599
Between you and me,

730
00:36:00,480 --> 00:36:02,360
behind closed doors,

731
00:36:04,440 --> 00:36:05,440
brother,

732
00:36:06,519 --> 00:36:07,519
the truth is,

733
00:36:08,119 --> 00:36:09,800
the tables turned long ago.

734
00:36:10,639 --> 00:36:11,639
Looking ahead,

735
00:36:12,079 --> 00:36:15,480
cross-strait politics will change.

736
00:36:16,440 --> 00:36:17,360
Ma Qi

737
00:36:18,159 --> 00:36:19,719
is crucial to me.

738
00:36:20,880 --> 00:36:23,320
I need an accurate assessment from you.

739
00:36:27,840 --> 00:36:29,000
I don't trust anyone.

740
00:36:29,559 --> 00:36:31,000
Only myself.

741
00:36:33,639 --> 00:36:34,440
That's that.

742
00:36:35,960 --> 00:36:37,039
Mission accomplished.

743
00:36:37,440 --> 00:36:39,320
It's time for Old Zhu to take his leave.

744
00:37:15,199 --> 00:37:18,039
Start the Fourth Division handover.

745
00:37:18,039 --> 00:37:18,800
Immediately.

746
00:37:24,960 --> 00:37:27,519
The Cultural and Trade Forum is near.

747
00:37:27,519 --> 00:37:28,320
For this forum,

748
00:37:28,320 --> 00:37:29,360
all the on-site events...

749
00:37:29,360 --> 00:37:30,679
were handled by your son.

750
00:37:30,840 --> 00:37:33,920
I'm the Taiwan, China Chamber's deputy.

751
00:37:34,159 --> 00:37:35,880
For a major event for the Chinese nation,

752
00:37:36,239 --> 00:37:37,360
I just have to be a part of it.

753
00:37:37,679 --> 00:37:39,239
It brings honor to the family, doesn't it?

754
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:42,960
It's pretty much all set now.

755
00:37:42,960 --> 00:37:44,280
Can't quit halfway.

756
00:37:44,519 --> 00:37:46,280
Once your treatment shows improvement,

757
00:37:46,280 --> 00:37:47,400
I'll have to rush back.

758
00:37:47,679 --> 00:37:48,360
Maybe by then,

759
00:37:48,360 --> 00:37:50,239
you'll see me on TV.

760
00:37:51,599 --> 00:37:52,360
Back then,

761
00:37:53,519 --> 00:37:54,719
I wasn't good at school,

762
00:37:54,719 --> 00:37:56,039
and was terrible at tests.

763
00:37:56,760 --> 00:37:58,920
Now this is my only way to make you proud.

764
00:38:00,760 --> 00:38:01,679
Pretty good, right?

765
00:40:48,880 --> 00:40:51,199
The mountain watching over you will fall.

766
00:40:51,800 --> 00:40:53,719
A third of his brain vessels are blocked.

767
00:40:53,920 --> 00:40:56,519
We might get a call to mourn him any day.

768
00:40:57,360 --> 00:40:59,079
I don't know if he mentioned it to you,

769
00:40:59,320 --> 00:41:01,800
but Project Abyss is being terminated.

770
00:41:03,360 --> 00:41:04,480
Scrapped entirely, in fact.

771
00:41:08,239 --> 00:41:09,360
No one told me anything.

772
00:41:09,719 --> 00:41:11,039
Well, I'm telling you now.

773
00:41:13,840 --> 00:41:15,039
We're old classmates,

774
00:41:15,559 --> 00:41:16,280
on the same side.

775
00:41:16,559 --> 00:41:19,760
So I want to give you a heads-up on this,

776
00:41:20,440 --> 00:41:21,960
so you can be prepared.

777
00:41:22,519 --> 00:41:23,559
What are you saying?

778
00:41:23,960 --> 00:41:25,000
What I mean is,

779
00:41:25,000 --> 00:41:27,599
don't leave Taipei for the time being.

780
00:41:27,800 --> 00:41:29,199
Wait for new assignments.

781
00:41:30,400 --> 00:41:31,320
Sticking with me

782
00:41:32,039 --> 00:41:34,440
is better than someone who doubts you.

783
00:41:38,440 --> 00:41:39,719
What about the mainland intelligence?

784
00:41:40,199 --> 00:41:40,840
Are we dropping all of it?

785
00:41:41,119 --> 00:41:42,719
That's for me to worry about.

786
00:41:47,199 --> 00:41:48,800
Is this an order from higher up?

787
00:41:49,760 --> 00:41:52,800
What I want is what the superiors want.

788
00:41:56,840 --> 00:41:58,079
What about the Cultural and Trade Forum?

789
00:41:58,960 --> 00:42:00,440
A lot of the supporting events

790
00:42:00,440 --> 00:42:01,519
are already halfway through.

791
00:42:03,639 --> 00:42:05,840
The Cultural and Trade Forum is starting.

792
00:42:06,360 --> 00:42:07,840
No matter who you send in the future,

793
00:42:08,599 --> 00:42:10,360
these events cannot be disrupted.

794
00:42:10,519 --> 00:42:11,320
This event is very important.

795
00:42:11,320 --> 00:42:13,559
That event isn't important at all.

796
00:42:14,199 --> 00:42:16,800
What I'm doing is much more important.

797
00:42:17,280 --> 00:42:18,360
It's good for you and me,

798
00:42:18,760 --> 00:42:20,320
even better for our superiors,

799
00:42:20,599 --> 00:42:22,000
and for Taiwan, China, and its people,

800
00:42:22,000 --> 00:42:23,480
it's infinitely better.

801
00:42:24,320 --> 00:42:26,960
Direction matters more than effort.

802
00:42:27,599 --> 00:42:28,880
If I were Old Zhu,

803
00:42:28,880 --> 00:42:31,360
I would've taken bolder steps back then.

804
00:42:32,039 --> 00:42:33,800
At all costs.

805
00:42:34,320 --> 00:42:35,800
The situation in Taiwan, China,

806
00:42:36,000 --> 00:42:37,559
and the cross-strait situation,

807
00:42:38,519 --> 00:42:40,320
might not be what they are today.

808
00:42:44,199 --> 00:42:46,639
Old Zhu would never say,

809
00:42:47,480 --> 00:42:48,840
"at all costs."

810
00:42:53,960 --> 00:42:54,960
I would.

811
00:43:08,480 --> 00:43:09,559
I'm Wang Kai,

812
00:43:09,559 --> 00:43:11,280
inviting you to watch the TV series

813
00:43:11,280 --> 00:43:12,199
Confrontation.

814
00:43:12,559 --> 00:43:13,599
Lin Kanshan has returned to the mainland.

815
00:43:13,599 --> 00:43:14,960
How did you let this happen?

816
00:43:14,960 --> 00:43:16,239
The moment he's back,

817
00:43:16,239 --> 00:43:17,280
arrest him immediately.

818
00:43:17,480 --> 00:43:18,119
Understood.

819
00:43:18,119 --> 00:43:19,280
They told me to pass along a message.

820
00:43:19,639 --> 00:43:21,239
Once the Cultural and Trade Forum ends,

821
00:43:21,239 --> 00:43:22,320
you're to return immediately.

822
00:43:22,320 --> 00:43:23,440
And what if I don't?

823
00:43:23,440 --> 00:43:24,599
With Huanyu launching into space,

824
00:43:24,599 --> 00:43:26,440
they're doing everything they can

825
00:43:26,440 --> 00:43:27,599
to obtain related intelligence,

826
00:43:27,599 --> 00:43:29,519
especially booster technology.

827
00:43:29,639 --> 00:43:31,119
Where is Ma Qi right now?

828
00:43:31,880 --> 00:43:34,239
Today is only the beginning.

829
00:43:34,239 --> 00:43:35,320
Here's to our cooperation.
